// INTRO 
"Coriander.Introduction": "Thanks for the save at the saloon, @. I get pretty overwhelmed by people sometimes, even though I know they mean no harm.",
// COMMUNITY CENTER BUNDLES  
"Coriander.JojaBegin": "Joja ruins everything, doesn't it? I don't even want to go into town anymore, seeing the warehouse is really upsetting.$25",
"Coriander.CCBegin": "That old building must be really important to the community if they've charged you with refurbishing it. Good luck!$22",
"Coriander.CCBus": "I'm pretty curious about the desert. I've never been, so it might be worth taking a bus trip to see...$3",
"Coriander.CCMinecart": "What? You can actually just jump in a minecart and ride it somewhere? That's wild! I wanna go!$7",
"Coriander.CCComplete": "Congratulations on finishing up that building project, @! I'm glad Joja didn't have the chance to buy it, after all!$14",
"Coriander.MovieTheater": "Oh! I love the movies, we should go! My treat! [809]$4",
// BIRTHDAYS
"Coriander.BirthdayReminder.Hector": "I snuck some fruit from Hector's greenhouse to make Ginger Beer from. I hope [LocalizedText Strings/DN.SnS:HeShe] likes it!$14",
"Coriander.BirthdayReminder.Val": "I wasn't sure what to get Val, to be honest. I did a little bit of research about blacksmithing and wound up getting them a crate of coal.$3",
"Coriander.BirthdayReminder.Roslin": "Roslin's a toughie, so I got her a stuffie. And I will continue to do so every year, forever.$11",
"Coriander.BirthdayReminder.Dandelion": "It's Dandelion's birthday, and I got her a bunch of different tea seed packets from different countries.$17",
"Coriander.BirthdayReminder.Arden": "Turns out, Arden and I have a common interest: seafood. So I ordered her a fancy branzino dinner. ...I think she may have also eaten the plate.$20",
// END OF SEASON
"Coriander.SpringEnd": "I won't pretend to know anything about farming, but I can say I'm looking forward to making Ginger Beer from your fruit!$6",
"Coriander.SummerEnd": "I'll miss beach weather, but that's okay. Time for sweater weather!$1",
"Coriander.FallEnd": "Are you ready for the cold, @? Hope you've got a good coat. Do you take it easy during the Winter?$4",
"Coriander.WinterEnd": "Finally, it's almost Spring again! I don't hate the cold, but I don't love it either. The overcast is so depressing!$22",
// SVE COMMUNITY DAY
"Coriander.CommunityCenter.1": "I was pretty nervous to show up, but everyone's too distracted to pay me attention. Which is for the best!$23",
"Coriander.CommunityCenter.2": "Pierre asked me about an ad read again. Maybe it's just the community spirit in the air, but I'm considering it.$20",
"Coriander.CommunityCenter.3": "Abigail said she had trouble dragging Sebastian here, but I think he loves it as long as he's hanging out with her and Sam!$1",
// FESTIVALS (DAY BEFORE)
"Coriander.EggFestival": "To be honest, I wasn't interested in the Egg Festival until Gus mentioned he was catering. The kids can have their egg hunt.$3",
"Coriander.FlowerDance": "I'm excited about tomorrow! Are you going to ask anyone to dance with you, @?$4",
"Coriander.Luau": "I'm really not sure what to bring to a soup that could have literally anything in it...$16",
"Coriander.MoonlightJelly": "We don't have Lunaloos in Port Drake, but we do have ... well, drakes, supposedly.$11",
"Coriander.SDVFair": "I considered offering to do a small show for the fair, but I know I'd probably get overwhelmed.$17",
"Coriander.SpiritsEve": "Spirit's Eve is tomorrow? Oh no, I almost forgot.$37",
"Coriander.IceFestival": "I'd love the Ice Festival if we cooked all that seafood after fishing it up. I don't know why they get thrown back.$3",
"Coriander.NightMarket": "I wonder if I can find any knickknacks from ZuZu or Port Drake at the Night Market. I love a good trinket.$1",
"Coriander.WinterStar": "I might have gone a little overboard with gift giving - what good does having Joja Records money do, otherwise?$6",
// ROMANTIC (NEGATIVE)
"Coriander.Breakup": "Oh - uhm, well. Th-thanks for everything, @... I, uh... I'm gonna... I'm gonna go, okay?$18#$b#Gonna go process. This was a relationship I have to mourn...$21",
"Coriander.Divorced ": "...I can't believe I actually trusted you to treat me any differently than the hundreds of thousands of people I performed for. Was this all just a performance for you?$5#$b#Leave me alone. I'm a notch in your bedpost, but you're just a line in a song.$5",  
"Coriander.SpouseFarmhouseClutter": "Oh, @! There's a lot of clutter around, would you mind tidying it up? I don't want to move your belongings where you don't want them.$2",
"Coriander.SpouseMonstersInHouse": "AHHHHHHHHHHHHHH MONSTERS-!? Quick, get 'em @! $37",
"Coriander.WipedMemory": "Uhm, sorry. Were you looking for an autograph or something? I don't do those anymore.$18#$b#You look familiar, though. Did you used to go to my shows?$17", 
// ROMANTIC (POSITIVE)
"Coriander.SpouseGiftJealous": "You're feeling pretty generous today, huh?$35", 
"Coriander.Stardrop": "I found this for you, @ - I wanted to show my love in something of a grand gesture. I hope you'll accept it!$33",
// RESORT
"Coriander.Resort.1": "Time for a beach daaaay!$22",
"Coriander.Resort.2": "Gus makes an excellent mocktail. I love that he makes sure I don't feel left out.$23",
"Coriander.Resort.3": "I could dunk myself in sunscreen and still be likely to burn...$3",
// GREEN RAIN
"Coriander.GreenRain": "What the heck is this? I've been all over the place and haven't seen rain come down this way!$37",
"Coriander.GreenRainFinished": "I hate rain, I hate rain, I hate rain, I especially hate WEIRD rain.$25",
"Coriander.GreenRain2": "Hector promised me that this rain is safe, but it still frightens me.$18",
// POLYAMORY 
"Coriander.MarriedMonogamousNPC": "Your partner is monogamous, @. So I'm not comfortable engaging in anything romantically with you.$2",
// TRASH REACT 
"Coriander.DumpsterDiveComment": "...@, do you need a bit of help?$18#$action AddMoney 1000",
// SLINGSHOT 
"Coriander.HitBySlingshot": "Owwwwww!$21#$b#What the heck, @!?$5",
// LOCATION ENTRIES 
"Coriander.VillageInn": "Hello, Harts!/It always smells so cozy here./What treats do you have today, Rosa?",  
"Coriander.BardHouse": "Time for some games!/I'm feeling like playing piano tonight.../Time to crack open an icy cold Ginger Beer!",
"Coriander.EastScarp": "Hello, world!/I wonder what I'll get up to today.../It's so pretty out!",
// LOW HEART
"Coriander.Generic.1": "Hey, @! Do you usually have headphones on when you're working? What kind of music do you listen to? I need tunes to focus, unless I'm writing my own.$11",
"Coriander.Generic.2": "I was cooking this morning, and I broke the egg yolk... What's even the point of breakfast if I can't dip stuff? Honestly, if that's the worst thing that happens today, I'll take it.$3",
"Coriander.Generic.3": "I was reading a really old sci-fi book about a meteorite crashing to a rural town and poisoning all the townsfolk. Not great bedtime reading while living... here.$20",
"Coriander.Generic.4": "Honestly, yeah, I have a lot of different hobbies! Games, books, music... I try really hard to vary my interests, I get pretty restless when I'm bored.$11",
"Coriander.Generic.5": "I have a really hard time keeping things clean. It's an active effort; I use notes and checklists to keep on top of things, besides the looming threat of someone wanting to come over...$10",
"Coriander.Generic.6": "I think part of what makes being a musician so hard is feeling self-conscious about people only liking my music because it's... loud, catchy? And not because it matters.$2#$b#I want it to matter.$25",
"Coriander.Generic.7": "Sometimes I fixate so hard on a task, I forget to eat. It's so easy to get lost in the things you love, but I've had to start keeping TV dinners around.$1",
"Coriander.Generic.8": "When I sit down with my keytar, I get really focused and keep playing even when I've got other stuff to do. I feel like I lose hours of my day ths way.",
"Coriander.Generic.9": "I really don't think there's any shame in being able to do a whole bunch of different things sort of mediocre.$0#$b#I can draw, and paint, and play music, and sing, and dance - only the music I'm exceptionally good at, but it didn't make learning those other skills any less fun.$1",
"Coriander.Generic.10": "I used to struggle with regulating my feelings, so over time I learned to let myself feel them and then process afterward. I've written most of my music after examining how I've felt once the intensity passed.$17",
"Coriander.Generic.11": "Today I cut up some photos and arranged them into a collage for a scrapbook. I have negative feelings about my career now, but I might appreciate looking at them in the future.$10",
"Coriander.Generic.12": "By the way, your lyre skills? Fantastic. It's so hard to learn niche instruments since there's so few people around to teach them.$1",
"Coriander.Generic.13": "Jacob's doing an incredible job of raising Eloise. She seems to be the smartest person in town, even though she's one of the smallest.$1#$b#I could listen to her talk about birds all day. I bought these binoculars and a book about birdwatching on a whim, I hope she's able to show me the ropes.$0",
"Coriander.Generic.14": "Moving here to revitalize the farm must've been like drinking from a firehose, huh? Well, that's okay. Happiness is worth the time it takes to learn new skills.$17",
"Coriander.Generic.15": "Is stargazing a hobby, or a coping mechanism? Either way, I do it a lot...$3",
"Coriander.Generic.16": "I was writing a song the other night, but got stuck unsuccessfully trying to rhyme the word 'cosmos'. Unless I'm talking about a guy named Carlos or nachos, it's not happening.$23",
"Coriander.Generic.17": "I appreciate how you don't look at me like I'm an alien. Most people do, even if they don't mean to.$17",
"Coriander.Generic.18": "My first job was as a pizza delivery driver; I did that while taking as many gigs as I could. I bought the pizza van after I quit and drove it all throughout my tour.$10",
"Coriander.Generic.19": "The trick to writing honestly is to pretend that nobody will ever read or hear it. Divorce yourself from judgement; don't let anyone stand between you and your creative works.$22",
"Coriander.Generic.20": "I'm replaying Kingdom Cross for the thousandth time. There's just something really comforting about themes of love and friendship acting as an actual power.$17",
"Coriander.Generic.21": "Spiro the Dragon is one of my favorite games. I love platformers - Hurdy-Gurdy and Bash Wombat are really good, too! Have you ever played them, @?$7",
"Coriander.Generic.22": "I can play all sorts of instruments, but mostly chordophones - guitar, bass. Haven't touched the violin in a while. Oh, and piano of course... but that's central to composition and music theory!$1",
"Coriander.Generic.23": "When writing lyrics, usually I get a specific line stuck in my head and work the rest of the song around lifting up that one bit. Especially if it's particularly poignant, or a really good rhyme.$3",
"Coriander.Generic.24": "The best wordplay usually comes to me out of nowhere, though it's pretty consistently after processing some big feelings. I have to scramble to get it written down otherwise it's gone.$10",
"Coriander.Generic.25": "Sometimes, a song starts as a lyric and moves outward. But other times, it's a specific musical riff on repeat until I can figure out how to use it.$0",
"Coriander.Generic.26": "Often, I'll just sit on the window bench and watch what's going on in the woods behind my house. It's rarely inspiring, but you can't be working on content ALL the time... Relaxing is important, too.$17",
"Coriander.Generic.27": "One thing I loved doing while on tour was visiting arcades. It's a lot of fun to play all sorts of different cabinets, and see different pinball machines!$1",
"Coriander.Generic.28": "I have a huge soft spot for stagecraft and general back-of-house aspects of performance. I got to share my vision for my backdrops, but it took a whole team to make everything work.$11",
"Coriander.Generic.29": "I'm fascinated by all things animatronic. I love them in parks - I visited a lot of theme parks while traveling - but I especially love the low-budget arcade ones. They're so spooky!$6",
"Coriander.Generic.30": "I'm convinced the pizza joint I used to work in was haunted. We had these animatronics that would bore into your soul if you stared at them too long...$18",
"Coriander.Generic.31": "Back when I worked at Bobby Bearclaw's Pizza Barn, we had this overnight security guard who was obsessed with one of our pinball machines. I think his name was Nic.$20",
"Coriander.Generic.32": "Bobby Bearclaw's Pizza Barn DID have really good pizza, which is the only way it stayed in business. The place was otherwise really dingy and I'm pretty sure it was a front for something.$2",
"Coriander.Generic.33": "A lot of discipline goes into creativity. Sure, it's great when inspiration strikes. But being consistent and showing up for yourself is what makes substantial progress.$14",
"Coriander.Generic.34": "When I was writing for Joja Records, I felt a lot of pressure to be productive. It warped my work ethic into something really unhealthy, because they were really willing to take advantage of me.$2",
"Coriander.Generic.35": "Consistency is underrated. Passion sparks the fire, but consistency keeps it burning when things get tough!$22",
"Coriander.Generic.36": "The keytar doesn't get the credit it deserves. It's a versatile instrument that's portable and makes me feel like I belong on a mural painted on the side of a van!$22",
"Coriander.Generic.37": "I keep a notebook of random lyric scraps - basically a diary, my eyes only. Some are profound, most are nonsense. Maybe one day, they'll find their place.$17",
"Coriander.Generic.38": "I'll always love synthesizers. They sound like 'the future'... I'm not sure how else to articulate the unique, electric sound.$11",
"Coriander.Generic.39": "When I see a broken arcade cabinet, I can't help but wonder if it's a fan-favorite busted from overuse or if it wasn't popular at all, and sat neglected...$2",
"Coriander.Generic.40": "I used to dream about headlining massive tours. Now that I've had that experience, I think I just want my songs to mean something to the people who hear them.$17",
"Coriander.Generic.41": "I think my favorite cabinet is The Grimpsons beat 'em up game. You can play as the whole family in four-player co-op. What's yours, @?$1",
"Coriander.Generic.42": "I'm always on the hunt for cartridges for my PixelPal Color. I got it on the road and have put so many hours into the little thing! I love finding games I haven't played or heard of before.$14",
"Coriander.Generic.43": "Do you have a PixelPal, @? I recently got a link cable to make some Pocket Critters trades and I was wondering if you played at all...$23",
"Coriander.Generic.44": "I burn through batteries so quickly... I need them for my PixelPal Color. Might as well start getting big bulk packs of them...$13",
"Coriander.Generic.45": "There's a new model of the PixelPal that has two screens, and can run games in 3D like the GameStation can. I haven't upgraded yet, though.$3",
"Coriander.Generic.46": "A big reason I learned the keytar was for stage presence. Being able to dance and move around engages the audience more than standing there on a typical keyboard.$0#$b#Mine has an accelerometer which let me control MIDI parameters by tilting the neck, so I can improvise mid-song if I'm feeling it!$1",
"Coriander.Generic.47": "MIDI stands for 'Musical Instrument Digital Interface'; it's basically the language that digital instruments use to speak with each other.$0",
"Coriander.Generic.48": "I've done most of the production work on my songs myself. I invested in a MIDI controller pretty early on, and I have a cutting-edge desktop serving as a digital audio workstation.$1",
"Coriander.Generic.49": "One of the arcade cabinets in my house was supposedly a plant by the Ferngillian government with the purpose of brainwashing people. With a story like that, I obviously needed it!$22",
"Coriander.Generic.50": "So, for proper pizza, the secret is the water. But also, the bottom has to be thin and crunchy while the crust is chewy and soft.$0#$b#The cheese to sauce ratio has to be exactly right, but the only way you'll know for sure is if you measure with your heart.$1#$action AddItem (O)DN.SnS_ZuZuPizza",
"Coriander.Generic.51": "ZuZu style cheesecake has to be rich. It has to be dense. And the graham crust has to be super buttery.$0#$b#You don't want to overdo it on the toppings. One aesthetic strawberry is perfectly fine; the whole dessert is tasty enough without extras.$1#$action AddItem (O)DN.SnS_ZuZuCheesecake",
"Coriander.Generic.52": "ZuZu style chowder always lifts me up when I'm feeling down. Especially since it's cheap and easy to make.$0#$b#I still think Port Drake style is better, since it's made to be thicker and it's delicious with crackers.$1#$action AddItem (O)DN.SnS_ZuZuClamChowder",
"Coriander.Generic.53": "Nothing beats the simplicity of a bagel with some lox on it. The secret is the water you're boiling the bread in, of course. Yup - good bagels are boiled, not baked.$0#$b#All you need is a smear of cream cheese, a cut of good salmon, and some onions if you're feeling particularly fancy. It's one of my favorite breakfasts!$1#$action AddItem (O)DN.SnS_ZuZuBagel",
"Coriander.Generic.54": "Oh, @! You look parched - have you been working hard today? Seems like it! How about we kick back and relax with some Ginger Beer?$17#$action AddItem (O)DN.SnS_GingerBeer",
"Coriander.Generic.55": "Oh, @! Just who I wanted to see. I just bottled my latest batch of Ginger Beer, I'd love for you to have one. Let me know what you think!$1#$action AddItem (O)DN.SnS_GingerBeer",
// HIGH HEART
"Coriander.Generic.56": "I hope that maybe Morris is a better person than he lets on, but I don't believe in 'deep down'. I kinda think all you are is just the things that you do.$13",
