// SEASONAL
"Coriander.Spring.1": "Spring is all about new beginnings, and I love that. I bet it's really busy for your farm, trying to get caught up after Winter. Good luck!$7",
"Coriander.Spring.2": "Do you cook often? I bet the home-grown crops must taste so good in all your meals.$0#$b#I'll trade you a homemade meal for fresh ingredients, @!$6",
"Coriander.Spring.3": "What kind of farming do you do, @? Do you mostly use a greenhouse, or do you focus on seasonal stuff more?$0#$b#I bet you make all sorts of fancy artisanal goods, too.$1",
"Coriander.Spring.4": "The one thing I don't like about the Spring and Summertime are the frequency of rain and storms. I'll take snow over thunder and rain any day.$2#$b#Being inside isn't the worst, but I'd much rather be spending the nicer half of the year out.$3",
"Coriander.Spring.5": "I don't even know what's in season this time of year. I just tend to pick the freshest looking stuff at the market.$3#$b#What are you growing, @? Got any insider info on what's tastiest right now?$1",
"Coriander.Summer.1": "My favorite icecream is a chocolate base, with marshmallow and caramel swirl, and chunks of chocolate. Bonus points if they're in fun shapes. What's yours, @?$1",
"Coriander.Summer.2": "I'm pretty proud of my wardrobe, but in particular, I go through a lot of swimsuits. There are just so many cute options these days.$4",
"Coriander.Summer.3": "Have you seen those rainbow shells that wash up on the beach? They catch the light so nice, and they've got a nice weight to them.$1#$b#Those mermaid pendants married folks wear look a lot like them, don't they? Maybe that's what they're made of.$6",
"Coriander.Summer.4": "You and I should visit ZuZu sometime, @. There's nothing like Summer in the city. It'll feel less oppressive now that you're not caught in the rat race.$10",
"Coriander.Summer.5": "I bet there's a lot of really solid fish you can catch this time of year. It's sushi season! I mean, it's always sushi season, but...$1#$b#Maybe avoid cooking with Pufferfish, though, I think that's a recipe for disaster.$3",
"Coriander.Fall.1": "I love how I can dress this time of year. It's not too cold, not too hot - perfect time to be fashion forward!$22",
"Coriander.Fall.2": "Cities have parks - I mean, ZuZu's got a big one in it's center - but it's not the same as all the foliage just being... everywhere.$3#$b#Yeah, yeah. Call me a leaf-peeper all you want, but it's because you're used to it. Let this city girl have nice things.$1",
"Coriander.Fall.3": "One of the things I've noticed about city folk is that the weather doesn't matter - the coffee is always iced.$3#$b#I don't mind either way, coffee is coffee, it doesn't do much for me in the energy department.$0",
"Coriander.Fall.4": "I do have a big appreciation for horror movie scores, especially the classic ones. Sometimes, minimal and chilling works a lot better than heavy orchestration.$0#$b#I think it's more memorable, too.$1",
"Coriander.Fall.5": "Okay, okay, but I've got an idea - so in ZuZu there were pop up Spirit's Eve stores around this time of year.$20#$b#What if you open one up in Spring? Hit the niche market of early costume preppers.$22",
"Coriander.Winter.1": "It's so cold out! I can't believe how quickly everything turned to snow - and it's STAYING snow!$37#$b#In the city, these light dustings turned to slush real quick, so snow was the enemy.$23",
"Coriander.Winter.2": "I knowwww, I know. City girl impressed by country winters. It's really trite. Just let me have this. Maybe the magic will wear off, maybe it won't.$4#$b#I know this is the plot of some of the cheesiest movies out there.$11",
"Coriander.Winter.3": "Maybe it's weird, maybe it's not. But I don't like heavy coats. I'd rather layer a whole bunch then wear like, one stupid puffy jacket.$3#$b#Makes me feel like I'm gonna fall over and get stuck in the snow.$2",
"Coriander.Winter.4": "It really does get chilly here, doesn't it? Well, that's alright. But there's plenty to look forward to; festivals, birthdays, quiet moments, springtime...$7",
"Coriander.Winter.5": "I'll take a snowstorm over a rainstorm any day... Nothing freaks me out more than thunder and lightning do.$2",
